1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,300
At 12:15 AM on September 26,

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:08,423
1983, a red siren illuminated a top-secret Soviet bunker outside Moscow.

3
00:00:08,503 --> 00:00:17,861
The radar screens confirmed what every officer dreaded: five American nuclear warheads were already in the air.

4
00:00:17,941 --> 00:00:30,320
Soviet protocol gave Lieutenant Colonel Stanislav Petrov exactly twenty minutes to authorize a retaliatory strike that would wipe three hundred million people off the face of the Earth.

5
00:00:30,399 --> 00:00:32,587
He had a direct line to the Kremlin.

6
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:35,611
His finger hovered over the confirmation switch.

7
00:00:35,691 --> 00:00:37,626
But instead of following orders.

8
00:00:37,706 --> 00:00:39,642
Petrov decided to trust a hunch.
